0..77 Comment "// The circle and the integers without a higher inductive type. The circle is"
78..153 Comment "// presented by a point, a loop and its inverse, with the two cancellations"
154..228 Comment "// as rules; its shape is a signature, and the integers are a model of it."
229..304 Comment "// A case over the circle is admitted when it computes one result from both"
305..380 Comment "// sides of each rule; the winding number does so only up to arithmetic, so"
381..457 Comment "// it is refused until the fold into the integers lands, and the equivalence"
458..482 Comment "// between them is owed."
484..561 Comment "/// The circle as a presented type: its rules rewrite constructor terms, so a"
562..604 Comment "/// word normalizes to the loops it winds."
